From: Kernel Security Review <security@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ext4: check reserved inode coverage for uninitialized groups

CVE: CVE-2018-10876
Upstream-Status: Pending [supplemental reserved-inode invariant guard]

The reserved-inode coverage check added by 501228470077 was moved
inside the initialized-bitmap branch by a149d2a5cabb. An invalid group
with INODE_UNINIT can bypass that check and request zeroing over the
reserved inode table. Perform the coverage check for both branches.
The no-free-block exception and full-table behavior remain intact.

This applies the invariant described by the original CVE fix and its
follow-up without disallowing lazy initialization of valid groups.

Upstream references:
https://git.kernel.org/linus/8844618d8aa7a9973e7b527d038a2a589665002c
https://git.kernel.org/linus/5012284700775a4e6e3fbe7eac4c543c4874b559
https://git.kernel.org/linus/a149d2a5cabbf6507a7832a1c4fd2593c55fd450

--- a/fs/ext4/ialloc.c
+++ b/fs/ext4/ialloc.c
@@ -1569,21 +1569,21 @@
 			goto err_out;
 		}
 
-		used_inos += group * EXT4_INODES_PER_GROUP(sb);
-		/*
-		 * Are there some uninitialized inodes in the inode table
-		 * before the first normal inode?
-		 */
-		if ((used_blks != sbi->s_itb_per_group) &&
-		     (used_inos < EXT4_FIRST_INO(sb))) {
-			ext4_error(sb, "Something is wrong with group %u: "
-				   "itable unused count: %u; "
-				   "itables initialized count: %ld",
-				   group, ext4_itable_unused_count(sb, gdp),
-				   used_inos);
-			ret = 1;
-			goto err_out;
-		}
+	}
+	used_inos += group * EXT4_INODES_PER_GROUP(sb);
+	/*
+	 * Are there some uninitialized inodes in the inode table
+	 * before the first normal inode?
+	 */
+	if ((used_blks != sbi->s_itb_per_group) &&
+	     (used_inos < EXT4_FIRST_INO(sb))) {
+		ext4_error(sb, "Something is wrong with group %u: "
+			   "itable unused count: %u; "
+			   "itables initialized count: %ld",
+			   group, ext4_itable_unused_count(sb, gdp),
+			   used_inos);
+		ret = 1;
+		goto err_out;
 	}
 
 	blk = ext4_inode_table(sb, gdp) + used_blks;
